WEBVTT

0
00:00.550 --> 00:02.330
<v Krista>In this video, we're talking about division</v>

1
00:02.330 --> 00:05.220
by zero and the fact that dividing by zero

2
00:05.220 --> 00:07.250
is actually undefined in math.

3
00:07.250 --> 00:09.630
Lets look at a couple of examples to illustrate

4
00:09.630 --> 00:11.440
why sometimes people get confused.

5
00:11.440 --> 00:13.100
In this first example here,

6
00:13.100 --> 00:16.810
we have fractions two over one times one over two.

7
00:16.810 --> 00:18.140
We want to multiply these together.

8
00:18.140 --> 00:19.820
Remember when we multiply fractions,

9
00:19.820 --> 00:21.770
we multiply the numerators together.

10
00:21.770 --> 00:23.660
So our numerators two times one.

11
00:23.660 --> 00:24.770
We get two.

12
00:24.770 --> 00:27.940
In the denominator, we have one times two or two.

13
00:27.940 --> 00:30.870
Two over two is equal to one and that's fine.

14
00:30.870 --> 00:32.060
But in this case,

15
00:32.060 --> 00:33.610
we multiply our numerators together.

16
00:33.610 --> 00:35.840
We have two times zero is zero

17
00:35.840 --> 00:38.130
and our denominator is zero time two.

18
00:38.130 --> 00:39.230
We also get zero.

19
00:39.230 --> 00:41.300
So comparing this to our first example

20
00:41.300 --> 00:43.210
where you have two over two is equal to one.

21
00:43.210 --> 00:45.770
You might say zero over zero is equal to one.

22
00:45.770 --> 00:47.260
But, in fact, that's not true.

23
00:47.260 --> 00:49.800
Zero over zero is not equal to one.

24
00:49.800 --> 00:51.610
It is undefined

25
00:51.610 --> 00:54.920
and that's because zero is a special number.

26
00:54.920 --> 00:56.910
We can't treat it exactly the same

27
00:56.910 --> 00:58.810
as we do non-zero numbers.

28
00:58.810 --> 01:00.470
In one of the ways, its not the same

29
01:00.470 --> 01:02.550
is that we can never divide by zero.

30
01:02.550 --> 01:05.010
So zero over zero is going to be undefined

31
01:05.010 --> 01:07.810
and even if we just have some constant value

32
01:07.810 --> 01:10.980
in the numerator and just zero in our denominator only,

33
01:10.980 --> 01:12.500
that's still going to be undefined.

34
01:12.500 --> 01:14.060
We can never do this.

35
01:14.060 --> 01:16.240
We can never have zero in our denominator.

36
01:16.240 --> 01:18.130
So this value is not equal to one.

37
01:18.130 --> 01:19.440
In fact, its undefined.

38
01:19.440 --> 01:20.700
And it doesn't matter what we might

39
01:20.700 --> 01:22.830
be multiplying by zero in our denominator.

40
01:22.830 --> 01:25.340
If we have a zero in our denominator, it will be undefined.

41
01:25.340 --> 01:27.520
So lets look at this other example here

42
01:27.520 --> 01:29.610
to show that this is also undefined.

43
01:29.610 --> 01:31.720
If we multiply our numerators together,

44
01:31.720 --> 01:35.060
we get three times zero times Y.

45
01:35.060 --> 01:37.030
Well, because we're multiplying by zero,

46
01:37.030 --> 01:39.610
we're still just going to get zero in our numerator.

47
01:39.610 --> 01:43.340
In our denominator, we have zero times X times four

48
01:43.340 --> 01:45.720
and it doesn't matter that we're multiplying by X and four

49
01:45.720 --> 01:49.230
because anything multiplied by zero is still zero.

50
01:49.230 --> 01:51.860
So we still end up here with the zero over zero

51
01:51.860 --> 01:55.750
and, of course, we know that that is undefined.

52
01:55.750 --> 01:57.630
Looking at this example over here.

53
01:57.630 --> 01:59.330
When we multiply our numerators together,

54
01:59.330 --> 02:01.300
we get AB times three,

55
02:01.300 --> 02:04.220
or in other words, 3AB in the numerator

56
02:04.220 --> 02:06.930
and in the denominator, we have zero times zero,

57
02:06.930 --> 02:08.310
which we know is zero.

58
02:08.310 --> 02:10.760
And here, even though we have a non-zero value

59
02:10.760 --> 02:12.540
in our numerator, 3AB,

60
02:12.540 --> 02:15.360
we still have a zero value in our denominator,

61
02:15.360 --> 02:17.360
which is not allowed and so we say

62
02:17.360 --> 02:19.590
that this is also undefined.

63
02:19.590 --> 02:22.500
We can never divide by zero.

64
02:22.500 --> 02:24.400
This here is not acceptable.

65
02:24.400 --> 02:26.410
So for all three of these examples,

66
02:26.410 --> 02:28.670
we can't come up with a real number answer.

67
02:28.670 --> 02:30.323
They're all undefined.